WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:01.570
All right.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.120
Familiar scenes on opening day at camp at the Browns' picturesque headquarters on the

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.710
Hiram College campus.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:00.000
Freddie Bottomer, veteran sports photographer, is the man behind the campus.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.280
Bill Shoal of the press and news moves in for a chat with Jim Ray Smith. The

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.460
plane dealer representative is Chuck Heaton. He talks with a new member of the

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:21.110
team, Sam Baker. Pictures help make stories. The Browns hire a staff of

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:26.280
photographers to take publicity shots and some 50,000 photographs will be

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.000
circulated to newspaper, magazine, and television outlets in a

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:42.720
years time. Rich Kreitling is ready to make his bid for a regular job. Bobby

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:53.160
Mitchell warms up. Ray Renfro is back for his ninth season. Sam Baker, acquired in

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.740
a deal with the Washington Redskins, takes over all of the Browns kicking

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.590
assignments.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:05.900
Jim Grainer handles the color commentary on the Browns' radio network.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:12.420
Jim is interviewing quarterback Milt Plum for his nightly television sports show.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.380
Speed is important in football.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:18.050
The Browns' candidates always are timed over the 40-yard route.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:21.590
Paul Bixler and Paul Brown watch the start.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:27.620
The timer is Eddie Finnegan, Western Reserve Athletic Director and noted track coach.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.000
George Finney enjoys this day.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:36.230
records the results. The hot days of late July and early August are rugged ones in the

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:41.900
life of a pro football player. Two sessions a day are held. Hiram is located in the heart

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:47.550
of the Brown fan interest and they take their football seriously. Visitors are welcome to

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:52.450
attend the workouts and hundreds are on hand every day. The Browns have three full weeks

00:02:52.450 --> 00:03:00.000
of work before the preseason schedule gets underway. The 1960 slate of six games starts

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.820
in Detroit and included

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.180
games in Pittsburgh, Akron, Los Angeles

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.240
and Portland, Oregon.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.270
One game was played in Cleveland.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.010
Five victories were wrapped up.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.010
The end of a long and distinguished career

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.690
came the day before the final preseason game.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.350
The player who wore

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.630
number 76 through 14 years

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.450
of pro football carefully

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.850
folds the jersey and lays it aside.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.470
The last charter member

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.610
of the Browns announced his retirement.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.000
Lou Groza achieved wide

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.140
acclaim for his offensive tackle play

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.020
and place kicking. He holds

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.960
many National Football League records.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.110
He scored 1,001

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.370
points during his career.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.140
When his playing days ended, Lou

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.120
moved into another post with the Browns.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.950
He was given an assignment as

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.250
assistant to personnel scout Paul Bixler.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:50.240
Lou traveled thousands

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.140
of miles watching college games

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.040
and visiting college practice sessions

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.140
and spent countless hours

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.980
studying reports from the Browns'

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.000
vast network of scouts around the

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:08.920
country. He signed many of the draft choices for the 1961 season. The season is on. The opener is

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:16.090
played at Philadelphia. The Browns kick off but get possession early on Bernie Parrish's

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:27.610
interception of Norm Van Brocklin's pass. Bernie makes a nice return of 31 yards.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.830
Touchdowns come fast when you have a fellow like Bobby Mitchell in your backfield.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:46.960
Bobby takes a flip from Milt Plum and shows his elusiveness on a 31-yard run to the season's first touchdown.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:58.710
A pair of rookies earned regular jobs in the defensive backfield.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.000
Don Fleming of the United States.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:05.200
of Florida was at left safety and comes up with another interception. He makes a

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:15.450
good return and then laterals to Galen Fiss. Jim Brown made a fast start toward

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:23.730
another big year. He gained 153 yards in the opening game. 17 came on this effort.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:36.130
Ted Dean was one of the season's prize rookies.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.350
He's number 35 in the Eagles' backfield.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:43.250
Ted takes a pass from Van Brocklin and goes for 31 yards.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.910
Jim Schaffner makes the tackle.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.360
Another run by Jim Brown.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.000
A block by Ray Rent.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:14.410
number 26 brings him loose as he rounds the corner Jim is away for 37 yards it's

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:22.020
Mitchell again will anyone catch him he's a very elusive ball carrier and it's

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:30.000
another touchdown on a 30-yard run Norm Van Brocklin said this would be his last season as

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:39.280
player and he made it a great one. He fires a pass to Bobby Walston for a 36 yard game.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:47.450
Jim Schaffner brings him down. Van Brocklin aims another one to Walston. The ball is right

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:58.090
on target and Walston makes a fine catch for a touchdown. The Browns won 41-24. The Steelers

00:06:58.090 --> 00:07:00.000
visit Cleveland for the first of six home runs.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:04.990
games for the third year in a row the Browns break their opening game

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:10.560
attendance record program sales are brisk as the Browns have many unfamiliar

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:18.780
faces familiar sights around the stadium souvenirs are plentiful a Sunday

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:23.790
afternoon businessman part of the crowd that number sixty seven thousand six

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:30.000
hundred ninety two the Theodore Roosevelt post 469 commanded by Lanny Holum

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:41.280
Participates in the traditional flag-raising ceremony a final warm-up by the offensive unit head coach Paul Brown

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:50.630
Defensive tackle Bob gain captain and offensive tackle Mike McCormick linebacker Walter Michaels

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.810
Defensive tackle Floyd Peters

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:59.340
Offensive guard Gene Hickerson the game is on

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:02.880
Plum fakes a handoff, sets up the pass,

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:11.170
and he fires to Gern Nagler for 25 yards.

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:15.300
Plenty of time for Plum to pick out his receiver on this play.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.000
It goes to Rich Kreitling.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.000
Kreitling, a second-year man from Illinois,

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.020
playing his first year as a regular.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:28.540
Bert Brechachar nips him at the ankles.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.000
Plum takes advantage of a blocker

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:39.500
by Prentice Scott, number 40, steps ahead and fires to Gurren Nagler. Another pass to Kreitling

00:08:39.500 --> 00:09:00.000
coming up. Kreitling has good speed and outruns the defender to go in for a touchdown. The Browns 28, Steelers 20. Dallas

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.980
was granted a National League franchise at the 1960 Winter Meeting. The Cowboys

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:11.290
used the Cotton Bowl for their home games. The Bowl is part of the Texas State

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:20.230
Fairgrounds, and the fair was going strong. So were the Browns and Bobby Mitchell.

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:27.810
Mitchell gathers in this player screen from Milk Plum, and there's no catching

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:30.000
Bobby. It's a 46-yard touchdown.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:39.900
down play. Eddie LeBaron moved from Washington to Dallas to quarterback the

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:46.980
Cowboys. Eddie tries a pass but Galen Fiss intercepts and gets back to the 42

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:58.290
yard line. A handoff from Plum to Mitchell. Watch Mitchell's sudden burst of speed.

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:07.830
He keeps the throttle open and goes all the way.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:16.700
A big moment for a big Texan.

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:20.430
Larry Stevens, rookie from the University of Texas,

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:22.830
was in a defensive tackle for the Browns.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:25.030
Larry intercepts LeBaron's pass.

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:27.910
Looks like a halfback as he makes it to the end zone.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:40.110
The second half kickoff, Dick Bielski makes it, and Mitchell will catch it.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:51.120
He'll do a tightrope dash along the sidelines and go all the way on a play that covers 90 yards.

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:05.930
an easy touchdown for gurn nagler no one is near gurn as he takes plums pass

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:15.750
and goes over browns 48 cowboys seven a rematch with the eagles in cleveland

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:22.140
the eagles first offensive play van brocklin gets good protection

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:26.920
he fires and walston makes the catch at the 20-yard line and goes over

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:35.660
A pretty play and a good advance.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:39.370
Mitchell circles back to take Plum's handoff

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:43.210
and wheels around his own left end to pick up 21 yards.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.500
Looks as if Plum is in trouble here.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.560
Apparently can't spot a receiver in the open,

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.490
but it turns out well.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.000
Big Leon Corbin.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.100
Clark makes the catch and shows some of the speed that made him an outstanding

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:20.190
college hurdler a few years ago. It's an 86-yard scoring play. Brown's long-distance

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:26.000
scoring punch comes into focus again. Jim Brown goes 71 for this touchdown,

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:29.760
and it gives the Browns a 22-7 lead.

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:36.190
But it's only the third period, and a 15-point lead is never safe in pro football.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:44.560
The Eagles strike back.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:48.420
It's a draw play, and Clarence Peaks takes Van Brocklin's hand off.

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:51.100
He breaks away for 57 yards.

00:12:56.490 --> 00:13:00.000
Bobby Franklin trips him up, and Peaks is downed at the center.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:07.550
seven-yard line. The Eagles scored two plays after Peaks run and come right back

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:13.160
for another touchdown a few plays later. Here it is. Tommy McDonald makes the

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:21.330
catch of Van Brocklin's pass. Don Fleming grounds the Eagle but not quite soon

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:30.000
enough. The Eagles scored again and at this point the Browns trail 28-22. Now it's the Browns turn

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.160
in this seesaw thriller.

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:33.780
This pass from Plum to Mitchell

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:35.260
puts them in position

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:36.520
to regain the lead.

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:47.710
The Eagles jam the middle

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:48.870
and stop Jim Brown,

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:50.850
but he doesn't have the ball.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.710
Mitchell takes a touchdown pass

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:54.990
that makes it 29-28.

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:00.000
Philadelphia starts another turn

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:05.220
drive, still plenty of time for trouble. It starts on this Van Brocklin pass to Pete Retzlaff.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:10.960
This was Van Brocklin's last game in Cleveland. He's now the new head coach of the Minnesota

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:21.800
Vikings. This is called a delayed roll-off pass, and it's hard to stop. Van Brocklin

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:26.100
flips the ball over the middle to Billy Barnes, and it's a 14-yard game.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:36.550
Paul Wiggin comes in from right hand to force Van Brocklin to unload the ball in a hurry.

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:41.460
The throw is short. The eagle receiver on the ground in the end zone and Don Fleming is alert

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:46.380
to make an interception and temporarily halt the Eagles.

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.860
The Eagles regain possession.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:50.760
Less than two minutes to play now.

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:53.680
And once more, Van Brocklin swings into action.

00:14:53.680 --> 00:15:00.000
Here's a 27-yard gain on a pitch to Retzlaff.

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:16.090
A pass to McDonald and another eight yards.

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:23.890
The official flag is bad news for the Browns.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:24.980
There it is.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.180
Bobby Franklin makes the interception,

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:30.000
but interference had been called and the Eagles

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:35.720
the ball. Only 10 seconds to play now and here's the thrilling wind-up to an

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:41.610
exciting wide-open game. A field goal by Bobby Walston gives the Eagles a 31 to

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:52.480
29 victory. A visit to Washington. The Redskin Band is a volunteer organization.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:58.260
They always present a good show. Hail to the Redskins is their theme song.

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:10.440
will mitchell be tossed for a loss here no it's the halfback pass a perfect throw to a sure-handed

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:21.100
target ray renfro makes the catch of the soft pass for the touchdown a touchdown pass from plum to

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:30.000
gern nagler gern whirls around the defender and is off ray renfro's downfield block is a big help

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:39.290
The Browns beat the Redskins 31-10.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:41.010
The New York Giants are next.

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:44.370
A record crowd sees this one.

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:47.970
A pair of field goals gives the Browns a 6-0 lead.

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:50.880
The Giants then start a touchdown drive.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:52.880
A short gain by Mel Triplett.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:57.420
Vince Costello makes the stop.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:17:00.000
Veteran Charlie Connolly returns to action after

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:09.570
long layoff. He passes to Joe Morrison. A little trouble stopping this fellow

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:22.560
until Bernie Parrish meets him head-on. Frank Gifford has been an outstanding

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:26.600
star for many years. He's number 16, the left half-back.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:33.720
Frank takes the handoff and fights his way to the 5-yard line.

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:45.010
It's Triplett again, up and over, and there's the touchdown signal.

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:49.080
A break for the Browns.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:53.940
Here goes Triplett again, but he forgets to hang on to the football.

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:58.160
Jim Schotner recovers and gets back a few yards.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:09.750
A good example of pass protection by Mike McCormick,

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:13.500
number 74 on the right side of the line.

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:15.360
He chops down the rushing giant,

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.440
Plum gets the pass away to Mitchell,

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:22.560
and Bobby reaches the five-yard line.

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:28.090
A great effort by Ray Renfro coming up.

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:30.000
The touchdown puts the Browns

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:42.480
in the lead. The Giants keep running Gifford and Triplett for short yardage. Here goes Gifford

00:18:42.480 --> 00:19:00.000
for 12 yards. The draw play. The handoff to Triplett. A gap in the middle and it's a 16-yard gain.

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:11.340
triplet comes right back. The middle is jammed this time, so Mel slides off to the right

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:25.380
and fights his way to the five. It's Gifford on a sweep to the right. A good block by Jack

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:27.550
Stroud. And Gifford goes over.

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:32.370
The Giants win 17-13.

00:19:34.420 --> 00:19:35.980
The Cardinals found a new home.

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:37.840
They represent St. Louis now.

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:41.650
Milt Plum shows he can throw that long ball.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.900
This one goes to Ray Renfro.

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:47.560
And Renfro, in his ninth year of pro football,

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:50.570
shows he still has a full measure of speed.

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:59.380
A pass to Nagler.

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:09.350
Gurren is bumped, but keeps his feet to stumble along for an extra seven yards.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:15.040
The Cardinals have a versatile offense and a halfback who can throw that ball.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:18.180
John Crow takes this lateral from John Roach.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:28.800
Crow passes to Joe Childress for a touchdown.

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:30.000
The Browns, 28.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:37.030
Cardinals 27 there were many exciting days in Forbes field in 1960 and here is

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:42.090
one of them Jim Schaffner's interception gets the Browns out of trouble early in

00:20:42.090 --> 00:21:00.000
the game the Browns are backed up to their own goal line but the

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.780
The Plum to Renfro combination gets them up to midfield.

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:07.110
Here are three straight passes to the sure-handed Ray.

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:44.080
Bobby Green isn't very big, but there's a lot of power in his right leg.

00:21:44.080 --> 00:21:53.450
Here is a 75-yard punt.

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:57.450
Can't identify this fellow without a number.

00:21:57.450 --> 00:22:00.000
Jim Brown carries out a fake perfect punt.

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:03.920
And fools Joe Lewis, number 71 of the Steelers.

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:10.600
Plum throws a long one and Mitchell grabs it and in one play the ball is back from where Green kicked.

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:19.850
Here's a play that fooled the cameraman.

00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:24.210
Plum pumps the ball as he looks for a receiver at the right.

00:22:24.210 --> 00:22:28.480
Shifts directions and throws to Rich Kreitling for a touchdown.

00:22:34.320 --> 00:22:36.400
It is fourth down and two for the Steelers.

00:22:36.520 --> 00:22:39.250
They're three points behind, and go for the touchdown.

00:22:39.940 --> 00:22:44.780
Lane hands off to Tom the bomb Tracy, and he goes wide to the right and over.

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:56.220
Browns are on the 24 after the kickoff, and now for a wild windup.

00:22:56.220 --> 00:22:59.600
This pass to Nagler moves the ball to the 40-yard line.

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:13.470
Another pass to Nagler takes it deep into Steeler territory.

00:23:13.470 --> 00:23:22.760
It's Gern's 10th catch of the game.

00:23:22.760 --> 00:23:25.820
Plum is rushed by George Tarasovic of the Steelers

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:28.150
on this play.

00:23:28.150 --> 00:23:30.000
He can't get the pass off and wisely

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:34.820
grounds the ball to stop the clock. The Browns lose 15 on the penalty, but it

00:23:34.820 --> 00:23:46.380
gives them time for two more plays. A pass to Leon Clark takes it to the

00:23:46.380 --> 00:23:57.460
Steeler 10. Time for just one more play now. The Browns rush back to the line of

00:23:57.460 --> 00:23:59.360
scrimmage. Plum hunts a receiver.

00:24:01.400 --> 00:24:21.860
throws to Clark past an excited youngster. It's incomplete. Steelers 14, Browns 10. The Browns

00:24:21.860 --> 00:24:30.000
visit St. Louis for the first time. Prentice Scott makes his first start in the Browns backfield. Here he

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:41.690
He goes for 14 yards.

00:24:41.690 --> 00:24:45.630
It's got again.

00:24:45.630 --> 00:24:54.740
The rookie runs for 9 more yards.

00:24:54.740 --> 00:24:57.560
The Browns shift to the forward pass.

00:24:57.560 --> 00:24:59.060
Plum throws to Gern Nagler.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:08.810
He does some fancy stepping, and it's a touchdown.

00:25:08.810 --> 00:25:13.130
Another pass, and another touchdown.

00:25:13.130 --> 00:25:19.760
Clark is the receiver in the end zone.

00:25:19.760 --> 00:25:23.570
The Cardinals have one of pro football's

00:25:23.570 --> 00:25:27.350
outstanding receivers in Sonny Randall.

00:25:27.350 --> 00:25:29.380
He takes this touchdown pass,

00:25:30.190 --> 00:25:35.450
And it's a tie game, 17 to 17.

00:25:35.450 --> 00:25:39.890
Washington at Cleveland.

00:25:39.890 --> 00:25:42.930
A nice run by Dick James and an early touchdown

00:25:42.930 --> 00:25:53.710
for the Redskins.

00:25:53.710 --> 00:25:55.910
Jim Brown, the league's leading ground

00:25:55.910 --> 00:25:58.320
gainer for the fourth year in a row.

00:25:58.320 --> 00:26:00.000
Looks like trouble for Plum.

00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:01.660
but he'll get out of it.

00:26:01.660 --> 00:26:05.290
Milt waits for Brown to get in the open, throws,

00:26:05.290 --> 00:26:21.510
and Jim does the rest.

00:26:21.510 --> 00:26:30.000
A shoestring catch by Mitchell and another fancy run by

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:49.140
speedy Bobby Vince Costello veteran linebacker watch Vince make the tackle

00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:55.320
on this play he's number 50

00:27:01.920 --> 00:27:03.660
Paul Wiggins, defensive right end.

00:27:04.310 --> 00:27:06.050
Jim Houston, defensive left end.

00:27:06.940 --> 00:27:10.420
They give Washington's Ralph Guglielmi a rough time on this play.

00:27:20.550 --> 00:27:22.650
Jimmy Schaffner, defensive right halfback.

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:27.440
Jim was a fine running back at Texas Christian,

00:27:27.790 --> 00:27:30.000
and he still gets chances when he makes interviews.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:52.850
interceptions. Members of the defensive unit leave the field. Bobby Mitchell. Bobby is developing into

00:27:52.850 --> 00:28:00.000
an outstanding receiver. He led the team in total catches with 45. Six went for touchdowns. And here

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:18.140
one of them. The Browns 27, Washington 16. The Bears come in for the last home

00:28:18.140 --> 00:28:25.640
game. Part of the big crowd on an extremely cold day.

00:28:30.250 --> 00:28:34.350
The new radio booths.

00:28:34.350 --> 00:28:39.810
Television and photographs are a big part of football.

00:28:39.810 --> 00:28:43.230
These men work from the roof of the stadium.

00:28:43.230 --> 00:28:48.710
About 50,000 feet of film is used to record the Browns games each year.

00:28:48.710 --> 00:28:55.750
Here are the men who make the pictures.

00:28:55.750 --> 00:29:00.000
The television crew with

00:29:00.160 --> 00:29:12.180
strategically placed cameras. Yours truly describing the game for the Browns

00:29:12.180 --> 00:29:22.970
Network. The hot dog salesmen do a nice business in cold weather. Here is George

00:29:22.970 --> 00:29:29.010
Breard, entertainment director, who arranges the halftime shows. Here's a

00:29:29.010 --> 00:29:30.000
youngster with talent.

00:29:40.460 --> 00:29:43.140
Leo Murphy, popular Browns trainer on the left.

00:29:44.390 --> 00:29:46.770
Maury Kono at left, handles the team equipment.

00:29:48.250 --> 00:29:51.130
The Browns cheerleaders, they come from Brush High School.

00:29:55.930 --> 00:29:57.250
Quarterback, Milt Plum.

00:30:03.680 --> 00:30:06.640
Offensive end, Leon Clark.

00:30:06.640 --> 00:30:16.290
They click for the game's first touchdown.

00:30:16.290 --> 00:30:25.730
Defensive halfback, Bernie Parrish.

00:30:25.730 --> 00:30:28.050
This is a big day for the defense.

00:30:28.050 --> 00:30:30.000
Parrish intercepts this pass.

00:30:30.220 --> 00:30:33.200
and is off on a 92-yard touchdown run.

00:30:33.810 --> 00:30:37.970
It's a record run with an intercepted pass for a member of the Browns.

00:31:06.940 --> 00:31:10.350
The Browns kick off and soon have another touchdown.

00:31:10.350 --> 00:31:26.250
Bobby Franklin, new safety man, makes this one on another interception.

00:31:26.250 --> 00:31:29.480
It's a rough day for Ed Brown in many ways.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:33.560
Paul Wiggins drops the Bear quarterback for a nine-yard loss.

00:31:41.320 --> 00:31:43.440
This is not a rerun of an earlier play.

00:31:48.200 --> 00:31:51.900
Franklin makes another interception and gets his second touchdown.

00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:16.100
more trouble for the bears an interception by parish a good return and the browns are in scoring position

00:32:32.080 --> 00:32:35.680
Prentice Gott, Oklahoma All-American and a Cleveland rookie.

00:32:37.240 --> 00:32:39.000
Gott's first touchdown as a pro.

00:32:40.880 --> 00:32:44.380
A handoff, a lot of drive, and six points.

00:32:49.160 --> 00:32:54.600
Franklin gets his name in the record book for most interceptions by a Cleveland back in a single game.

00:32:55.120 --> 00:32:56.640
Here is his third of the day.

00:33:15.520 --> 00:33:17.520
Brown's 42 bears nothing.

00:33:17.520 --> 00:33:22.500
Brown's fans are faithful fans.

00:33:22.500 --> 00:33:29.800
A crowd of more than 38,000 stayed to the finish of a one-sided game despite unpleasant weather.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:34.080
drifted out of the exits and into the snowstorm that hit midway through the

00:33:34.080 --> 00:33:41.050
game. The crowd total pushed the season attendance to 338,000 and the Browns

00:33:41.050 --> 00:33:46.070
maintained their season average of more than 56,000 per game for the third

00:33:46.070 --> 00:33:52.040
straight year. To fans everywhere, the Browns management extends its sincere

00:33:52.040 --> 00:33:57.620
thanks for their loyal support throughout the year. The championship

00:33:57.620 --> 00:33:59.480
season ended in New York.

00:34:00.890 --> 00:34:06.530
The Giants take a 7-0 lead on the first play after the opening kickoff on Dick Lynch's interception.

00:34:13.180 --> 00:34:15.140
A 23-yard scoring play.

00:34:17.490 --> 00:34:22.350
Charlie Connolly to Kyle Roat, and the Giants take a quick 14-0 lead.

00:34:25.970 --> 00:34:28.390
There will be plenty of scoring before this one is over.

00:34:28.930 --> 00:34:30.000
The Browns get into the afternoon.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:33.810
on this 25-yard pass from Plum to Renfro.

00:34:33.810 --> 00:34:45.200
Connelly doesn't always get his passes off.

00:34:45.200 --> 00:34:49.650
Jim Houston drops him for a 7-yard loss on this attempt.

00:34:49.650 --> 00:35:00.000
A pass over the middle.

00:35:00.190 --> 00:35:05.390
And Mitchell's speed gets another six points for Cleveland, a 64-yard play.

00:35:05.390 --> 00:35:25.490
Lee fakes a pass to his left end, finds Rote open in the end zone,

00:35:25.920 --> 00:35:30.000
and it boosted the Giants' halftime lead to 27-21.

00:35:30.510 --> 00:35:34.390
And they increased it another seven points right after the second half kickoff

00:35:34.390 --> 00:35:39.200
on a 70-yard pass from Connolly to Bob Schnellker.

00:35:46.190 --> 00:35:49.150
Don Fleming and Jim Schaffner trail him into the end zone.

00:35:56.580 --> 00:36:00.000
The Giants are within field goal range, but Pat Summerall's

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:22.560
is short. Bernie Parish makes the return. Lateral to Vince Costello adds a few yards.

00:36:30.120 --> 00:36:35.760
Time is running out, but the Browns refuse to fold.

00:36:35.760 --> 00:37:00.000
Plum hits Renfro with another pass, and Jim Brown swings into action. Jim now becomes

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:20.360
a receiver makes the catch and turns on the power he scores finally tries to pass to alex webster

00:37:20.360 --> 00:37:30.000
but paul wigan tips the ball and hangs on for the touchdown that puts the browns ahead the giants are

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:35.590
gambling now. It's fourth and ten, and Don Chandler fakes a punt. The Browns are not

00:37:35.590 --> 00:37:46.910
caught off guard. Dave Lloyd hauls Chandler down. The game's last touchdown. Another interception

00:37:46.910 --> 00:37:59.620
by a lineman. Bob Gain makes this one and runs it over. The Browns, 48.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:00.900
Giants 34.

00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:05.060
The victory gave the Browns a second-place finish

00:38:05.060 --> 00:38:07.140
in the National Football League's Eastern Division

00:38:07.140 --> 00:38:08.780
and sent them to Miami

00:38:08.780 --> 00:38:10.620
for the first playoff bowl game

00:38:10.620 --> 00:38:11.760
in the Orange Bowl.

00:38:12.250 --> 00:38:14.710
The team was quartered at the Monte Carlo Hotel

00:38:14.710 --> 00:38:16.430
for a week prior to the game.

00:38:16.980 --> 00:38:19.160
The usual work schedule of morning meetings

00:38:19.160 --> 00:38:21.260
and afternoon practices was carried out,

00:38:21.480 --> 00:38:23.260
but there was time for fun.

00:38:23.710 --> 00:38:25.090
Swimming in the hotel pool

00:38:25.090 --> 00:38:27.050
with the blue waters of the Atlantic Ocean

00:38:27.050 --> 00:38:27.690
in the background,

00:38:28.270 --> 00:38:30.000
and many of the players' wives

00:38:30.090 --> 00:38:47.540
made the trip. The season's final workout the day before the game. Eddie Ulinski directs the

00:38:47.540 --> 00:38:55.510
calisthenics. The Browns had home state support from the Barberton High School band. They provided

00:38:55.510 --> 00:38:57.490
pregame and halftime entertainment.

00:39:03.450 --> 00:39:09.100
The opening kickoff by the Lions' Jim Martin.

00:39:09.100 --> 00:39:17.310
Jim Brown makes the return.

00:39:17.310 --> 00:39:20.460
The season ended the same way it began.

00:39:20.460 --> 00:39:23.910
Here goes Mitchell on a long-distance gallop.

00:39:23.910 --> 00:39:26.150
88 yards to a touchdown.

00:39:30.760 --> 00:39:44.470
Gern Nagler makes a key block, but failure to convert after this touchdown cost the Browns a tie.

00:39:44.470 --> 00:39:51.030
The Lions win 17 to 16.

00:39:51.030 --> 00:39:59.730
Pageantry prevailed as the Orange Bowl committee went all out to make this first playoff bowl venture a success.

00:40:00.190 --> 00:40:08.680
float circle the field at halftime, going hand-in-hand with the best show in football.
